## RULE 37: DISK C:, CACHE CLEAN AND THE ONE-GO ORDER (owner, 2026-11-09)
C: reached 0 GB free (Claude temp folder) and commands began to fail. Owner order: empty C: properly, delete cache files. Cleaned only tool caches (pip, npm, uv, puppeteer, old Temp items; the Claude temp folder is kept): 0.0 -> 1.30 GB free. Not touched without the owner: Downloads 20 GB, .cache codex-runtimes/huggingface/whisper models (re-download), .claude/projects transcripts 5.6 GB, AppData Local Packages. Heavy output always goes to D:. Same day order (one message): add the cast voices to the ElevenLabs account myself (skip if the API needs no add), generate the whole audio in en/hi/mr once (cap, job key reuse), start the Flow work for shots 7 and 9 in parallel, recheck full size myself, then start the render; audio must not cause sync problems with the clips (measure real mp3 seconds against each slot before any mix).

## RULE 38: AUDIO FIT IS MEASURED, NOT ESTIMATED (2026-11-09)
Words-per-second of the text does not predict clip length: batch 1 (32 clips) showed 19 over their slot, up to 2.6x; the voices speak about 1.7-2.4 words per second (about 0.065-0.09 s per character). ElevenLabs voice speed 1.15 had no effect on eleven_v4 or multilingual_v2 (pilot, 52 credits). The only levers that work: shorter text, local atempo of the wav copy (accepted mp3 never touched), longer slots. Before any full paid run: one real line per voice, measure seconds per character, size every line to slot x allowed tempo, owner approves the shortened text, then run once. voice_cast.py: `fit_report.json`, `latest_ok` (newest clip per line id), speed in the job key.

## RULE 39: AUDIO WINDOWS AND SPOKEN TEXT v2 (owner go, 2026-11-09)
Spoken text of reel 1 = voices/FINAL_TEXT_v2.md/.json (also written into shots.json; backup shots.json.bak_pre_v2text). The scripted time_range is only the SPEAKING window; every shot is 6.6-10.1 s, so the audio window is wider: narrators run to the next line or shot end minus 0.25 s, characters keep their start and may end 0.6 s after the scripted end, the narrator of shots 6/8/9 starts at 4.3/5.1/5.9 s. Windows are stored in FINAL_TEXT_v2.json (start_s, window_s); shots.json time_range was NOT changed (video prompts depend on it), so the Gate D mix must read the windows from that file before any mix. Seconds per character measured: narrator 0.07-0.10, Brahma hi 0.11-0.14 (slow voice, keep Brahma hi lines under 35 chars), others 0.07-0.09. Export (voice_cast.py export) trims edge silence, measures tempo on the trimmed wav, MAX_TEMPO 1.15, writes fit_report.json. Result 2026-11-09: 54 of 54 clips fit (45 natural, 9 sped up by at most 1.074); credits used 1172 of cap 3000. A baseline for text changes is ALWAYS the text in shots.json, never the older approval_sheet csv (that mistake regressed 8 lines once).

## RULE 40: RENDER PRE-FLIGHT URL CHECK AND KEEP THE ERROR TEXT (2026-11-09, render S009 failed 3x)
Before ANY paid Colab session: curl every external download of the setup from this PC (free, 10 s): the pinned Wan2GP git clone, every URL in requirements.txt (today chumpy-0.71 from a GitHub release answered HTTP 504, also from the PC, while githubstatus said all operational), the model files. Any non-200: do not start a session. The runner downloads only timeline.txt and gpu.csv, so setup errors must be written into timeline.txt (sh_retry now writes the pip log tail). A blind retry is not a fix: find the cause first. Details: MISTAKES_AND_LESSONS W10-W12.

