## RULE 42: AUDIO FITS THE EDITORIAL LENGTH, NOT THE CLIP (owner reel 1 finish, 2026-11-09)
The reel cuts every shot at editorial_duration_sec (reel 1: 6,5,7,8,8,7,7,8,8,6 = 70.0 s); the clip tail (handles) is trimmed away. RULE 39 sized the voice windows to the whole clip and was WRONG for 14 of 54 lines. Correct basis: every voice line ends at least 0.1 s before the editorial cut (Gate D VO_OVERFLOW_ERROR), dialogue keeps its scripted start, one atempo per shot up to 1.15. Tools: director/build_vo_tracks.py (pack_shot: pure packing + one wav per shot per language, voices/<pack>/vo/<lang>/SHOT-nnn.wav) and director/build_final_reel.py (cuts + Gate D checks + mix + burned captions + loudness correction, one reel per language, NO music). Eight lines were rewritten shorter and regenerated (002-N hi, 003-D2 hi/mr, 005-D1 hi, 006-N en/hi/mr, 007-N mr). Script-level retention findings (narration density, dead air between scripted lines, shot 10 anchor/mouth) are WAIVED by owner order for the finished reel and written into the build report. Caption size is the engine default (34 px at 1080 w, core/captions.py BASE_PX_1080): small on a phone, owner decides.

## RULE 43: BACKGROUND SCORE PHASE (owner, 2026-11-09)
Scope: background music ONLY (no SFX, no voice work), BACKEND ONLY (never ui/), real reel 1 (Kalika Puran bhag 1, 10 shots, 70.0 s, 3,360,000 samples). Code lives in `anime_studio_merge/score/` (cue_sheet, plan_check, gate_d_bridge, note_writer, ableton_build, audition) with skill `.claude/skills/score-reel/SKILL.md` (do not redesign) and strict checklist `research/SCORE_BUILD_CHECKLIST_STRICT_2026-11-09.md`. The only stops are the owner gates M0 (bible), M1 (plan), M2 (preview); no Ableton write before M1; no commit or push without the owner. (1) STUDY FIRST: read the owner's curated docs yourself (core/, `D:\ableton claude\CLAUDE.md` 15 MCP rules, PLAYBOOK, README, serum-mcp docs, server.py) before building; do not hand the reading to an agent and trust the report. (2) Coders and reviewers are Haiku MEDIUM, different agents, one writer per file; I triage every finding against the file, the coder fixes, one re-review (rule 8). Writing work (plan, `why`, Serum briefs, extra reviews) uses Nemotron Super via the NVIDIA 14-key scheduler in slices of about 10 KB (OpenRouter key expired); plan_check validates what it writes. (3) Voice windows from FINAL_TEXT_v2.json are PERMISSION, not speech: `retention.last_speech_end_s` (69.8 s) is the last scripted word, `last_voice_end_s` (70.0 s) the end of the last window; both white-outs (43.083 s, 60.0 s) fall under voice, so both hits are low band. (4) Ableton: read before mutate, readback after, unsupported operations (automation points, notes into the arrangement, clip names on create) are recorded as manual or worked around by a designated route, never faked; the open Live set must be empty at 60 BPM (clock mode) before the build.

## RULE 44 (MAIN RULE OF THE MUSIC PHASE): THE STYLE IS THE MAIN THING (owner, 2026-11-09)
The owner's music style research is why all the files were given: the Anirudh and Sai Abhyankkar Style Study (Claude doc https://claude.ai/artifact/GA43TUfaKAxzBJRD1cDFiP, read it through the Claude Docs connector, `read` ref project GA43TUfaKAxzBJRD1cDFiP), the "Style" section of `.claude/skills/score-reel/SKILL.md`, and the curated folders (`reel score/`, `core/`, the Ableton and serum-mcp docs). Every musical decision (bible, themes, tempo and genre, plan, notes, Serum briefs, mix) must follow that style FIRST; code, checkers and gates serve the style, never the other way round. If a convenience, a test or a rule seems to fight the style, stop and ask the owner; the style wins. The study must be read in full before any bible or plan work, and the draft bible (written from SKILL.md only on 2026-11-09) is a guess until it is checked against the study line by line. Nemotron Super and every agent that writes plan or briefs gets the style study text in its prompt.

## RULE 45: STYLE DECISIONS FROM THE STUDY (owner, 2026-11-09)
Style study + scoring plan saved in `reel score/` and `anime_studio_merge/research/` (STYLE_STUDY_Anirudh_Sai_2026-11-09.md wins on style; SCORING_SYSTEM_PLAN on system; the plan words "raga" and "Sa" are void, no ragas). Owner answers: (1) genre colour MAY change at a shot boundary inside an act when the BPM stays the same (study: BUILD 128 = hypnotic techno SHOT-003, melodic techno SHOT-004, club + folk groove SHOT-005); BPM still changes only at act changes. (2) Vocal horn / chant = a Serum formant stand-in marked TEMPORARY until the owner gives a recording. (3) A/B test of 0-18 s at gate M1: A = modern hybrid cinematic, B = electronic (study). (4) Drums and folk percussion = Ableton stock Drum Rack only. Coders Haiku MEDIUM, reviewer Haiku HIGH, I observe and correct.
Amendment 2026-11-09 (owner): any sample, loop or instrument already in the owner's Ableton browser (built-in packs and the owner's own libraries) may be searched and used where it fits the style best, incl. drums, folk percussion and vocal chant packs (a fitting library vocal replaces the Serum stand-in). Still music only (no SFX used as SFX) and never a piece of a film or song recording.

## RULE 46: CAPTIONS OF THE FINISHED REEL (owner, 2026-11-09)
Captions = the SPOKEN words of each language (subtitles; the writer title cards only with --title-cards). Font Mukta ExtraBold (styles/fonts, OFL) + Noto fallback, about 60 px at 1080 wide (80 at the 1440 play width), white with dark outline, ONLY the word being spoken yellow #FFD400 (one ASS event per word, director/build_final_reel.py style_colours), max 6 words per card, at most 2 lines with BALANCED wrap (core/caption_text.py, no orphan word), Reels band 0.50-0.65 for both Reels and Shorts, SRT+VTT sidecars per language. The ASS family must be the font file's own family name (name ID 1: "Mukta ExtraBold"); with plain "Mukta" libass silently drew a system font. Check burned captions on real frames (contact sheet), never only the .ass text. Open: face boxes (captions can sit on a face in close-ups).
Amendment 2026-11-09 (owner handoff research/HANDOFF_REEL1_TO_MUSIC_2026-11-09.md): RULE 43 (3) is corrected: FINAL_TEXT_v2.json windows are permission windows only (wrong for 14 of 54 lines, rule 42). The score reads REAL speech from flow_outputs/anime_kalika_puran_bhag1/voices/pack_opus_high_20261108_v4_deva/vo_{en,hi,mr}/vo_tracks_report.json (line start/end from the shot start). Score against final_reel1_v3 only; music plugs into build_final_reel.py BGM slot (None today) via gate_d_bridge manifest; rebuild into final_reel1_v4.

## RULE 47: ONE SHARED PER-LANGUAGE TIMELINE (music session spec, owner go, 2026-11-09)
All languages share ONE picture timeline (one video, one audio track per language, one score). `<pack>/editorial_by_lang.json` (director/editorial_by_lang.py) adds frames the clips already have at the END of a shot (last shot: START only) so the slowest language speaks at natural speed: each shot = the largest need of all languages, whole beats for shots inside an act with a groove (reel 1: 3,4 at 128 BPM, 6,7,8 at 176), no rounding for the last shot of an act or the 60 BPM acts, capped by spare frames, voice speed-up at most 1.03x. Missing file = the old lengths. Both build_vo_tracks.py and build_final_reel.py read it. Freeze it before music gate M1; any later change is told to the music session. No voice regeneration and no render for this (owner). Reel 1 result: 72.833 s (1748 frames), final_reel1_v4, every voice 1.00x.

## RULE 48: MUSIC PRODUCTION QUALITY (owner, 2026-11-09)
Owner rejected stock-synth sketches and default Ableton patches ("sounds shit"): never send the owner a stock-synth or init-patch sketch as music again. Sound = produced, royalty-free samples from the owner's libraries (D:/Sounds of KSHMR Vol 4, D:/Producion class: KSHMR Vol 5 Dharma vocals/war horns/sitar/flute, Indian Perc Bagal Bachha, PML Melodic House + Afro House, 678 Serum presets) plus real Ableton presets for MIDI themes (never init patches). Timing engine stays (cue_sheet, plan, plan_check, note_writer). Samples are conformed offline (ffmpeg rubberband) to the section BPM and to D minor, cut on the reel clock, gated under voice, logged in sample_log (monetisation proof); words/lyrics never used. KEY: every tonal sample key is MEASURED (chroma), only D minor / F major, shift max 3 semitones else rejected, stems re-measured; modal colours only from MIDI themes. Every note/chord is checked by score/harmony_check.py before the owner hears it. Mix target: sidechain bass/pads to kick, bus glue + limiter, low-cut non-bass, 1-4 kHz dip, mono-safe, 15-21.5 dB under voice. Computer use for the Ableton export needs the owner to approve the access dialog (denied once 11-09). Series guide: research/MUSIC_PIPELINE_GUIDE_SERIES.md (update when the route changes). Coders Haiku medium, reviewer Haiku high.

## RULE 49: MUSIC ROUTE THAT WORKED FOR REEL 1, AND THE SFX PROBLEM (owner, 2026-11-09)
(1) Score = owner library samples chosen by score/sound_select.py (per slot: category/genre folder, BPM within 12% incl. half/double time, MEASURED key D min/F maj with shift <= 3 st, no words, audio-feature scoring, top 3 conformed 6 s snippets, SELECTION_BOARD.md, swap with --set SLOT=RANK) and built by score/stem_builder.py (whole-bar loops, frame-exact cuts, voice gate, sidechain, per-window gain riding to 15-21.5 dB under voice, sample_log = monetisation proof). (2) Indian + modern blend in EVERY section (owner): Indian slots take ONLY files whose name/path has a whole-word Indian instrument (tabla, dhol, sitar, flute, bansuri, shehnai, santoor, chant, hum, war horn, conch...), never by pack name alone, no 'mantra' (words); modern carries beat/bass/chords. (3) Bass keys: the chroma key estimator is blind below 65 Hz; bass falls back to 808/sub one-shots pitched to the nearest D with |shift| <= 5 st (f0 by autocorrelation). (4) Harmony: score/harmony_check.py before the owner hears anything; reel 1 ended at 10 flags, all kept on purpose (voice-gate theme cuts, Kamadeva chaos, Shiva crawl). Checker rules: no octave partner on the pad, melody notes are not chords in 3c, Phrygian bII a minor 9th or more over a D pedal is the colour. (5) Verify levels yourself from the written files (an agent once reported the target value as the measurement). (6) Ableton MCP cannot clear notes of an existing clip: delete Session clips by hand (computer use), then rewrite; Session clips override the arrangement until Back to Arrangement. (7) Reels with music: ffmpeg amix of voice audio + score, video stream copy -> final_reel1_v5. (8) OPEN: the reel sounds jumbled because the H3 model SFX are as loud as the voice (gaps -18.6 dBFS vs voice -18.4); the owner's Adaptive Reverse Engine pack (M4L reverse-swell effect) does not solve that. Proposed: per-shot SFX study, keep key hits, voice > hits > music priority mix, 1-4 kHz carve; needs owner go (changes rule 43 'keep model SFX').

## RULE 50: MIX IN ABLETON, MEASURE RIGHT, NAME EVERY RENDER (owner, 2026-11-09)
(1) Owner: the reel mix is done IN ABLETON (set score/ep1/kalika_reel1_score Project), never only in code outside: raw stems (research/_export_ableton_stems.py -> ableton_stems/) on audio tracks, EQ Eight per track, Compressor sidechains (MUSIC group <- VOICE, SFX <- VOICE, bass <- groove), Main Glue + Limiter, export by computer use (ctrl+shift+r, Render Length 19 bars, trim to 72.833 s after). (2) Every render gets its own name (renders/ableton_mix_<lang>_rN.wav), never replace, until the owner approves one; every try logged with settings + numbers. (3) Measuring: NEVER mute the VOICE fader to get the bus (it also removes the sidechain key; r1-r3 were wasted). Bus = mix render minus a voice-only render (MUSIC and SFX faders at 0). (4) Compute settings from one split measurement (music / SFX / voice levels in speech and gaps) instead of blind tries (owner: stop wasting). (5) EQ Eight via MCP: band-8 filter type needs 0.86 (0.857 lands on High Shelf); frequency x = ln(f/10)/ln(2200); gain (g+15)/30. Loading a device by browser double-click goes to the SELECTED track: select Main in Arrangement first. (6) Model SFX: keep only script-cue hits (short), mute model tones/mumble, beds 22 dB under voice (score/sfx_study.py + reel_mixer policy). Result reel 1: final_reel1_v7_ableton.

## RULE 51: CAPTIONS v2 FOR REELS/SHORTS (owner, 2026-11-09; amends rule 46)
Spec: anime_studio_merge/research/CAPTION_SPEC_v2_REELS_SHORTS_2026-11-09.md, code director/build_final_reel.py. Export 1080x1920 (lanczos, centre crop of the 768x1344 picture). Burn with `ass=...:fontsdir=styles/fonts:shaping=complex` ONLY: simple shaping broke every Devanagari conjunct (����?���1��?�r�_ shown as �����1�r�_) in v4-v7. Mukta ExtraBold 112 px en / 104 px hi-mr, outline 9, shadow 4; cards en <= 4 words (balanced 2 lines), hi/mr <= 3 words and 18 chars; \an5\pos(510,1290), bottom line fixed for 2-line cards; safe zone x 90-930, y 250-1420 (Reels/Shorts UI: top 250, bottom 500, right 150); active word green #3CFF4E + 108% pop (yellow vanished on gold scenes). Caption-only spelling fixes live in CAPTION_FIXES (voice text untouched): hi SHOT-003-D1 ����?�_�_�1��?�,, SHOT-010-D1 �-�������?. Check on real frames every time (contact sheet + conjunct crop). Reel 1 result: final_reel1_v8b.
# MISTAKES AND LESSONS (Anime Studio, written 2026-11-09)

Every big mistake that cost compute, time or effort, with the cost where it is known, the root cause, and the rule that now stops it. Honest on purpose: "we" includes me (Claude). Read this before any render, any Flow batch, or any agent launch. Rules in `blot.md` are cited as R<n>. Costs marked "unknown" were not measured.

## 1. Cost at a glance (reel 1, Kalika Puran Bhag 1)

| Item | Cost |
|---|---|
| Colab units: balance 187.61 before the first attempt, 178.61 after the finished render | 9.0 units in total |
| of which the useful render (all 10 clips) | 6.25 units |
| of which wasted on 4 failed starts (attempts 1, 2, 3, 5) | about 2.75 units |
| Opus writer stage lost its first 90% of the answer (rule R23) | 2.62 USD |
| Claude weekly limit reached on 2026-11-08 (resets 2026-11-12 15:30): no Opus or Sonnet CLI calls for days | planning and review capacity |
| Keyframes: 20 final images needed about 6 rework rounds and 4 agent generations | many hours, about 150 Flow submits |
| The first T0 test (2026-11-05): six clips rendered, then LOST because the final download failed | one full G4 session, plus an A100 re-render that also failed |

## 2. Compute mistakes (money)

| # | Mistake | What it cost | Root cause | Fix / rule |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| C1 | 2026-11-05 T0 run: the results folder did not exist locally, the final download failed, the runner then stopped the VM; six finished clips were lost | a full G4 session of rendering, a second session | clips were fetched only at the very end, the local folder was never created, the download step was not tested | R29: every clip is saved to the PC the minute its shot ends (`fetch_ready`); folders are created before use |
| C2 | The A100 re-render of those clips failed: Hugging Face HTTP 429 on the model download, then a hang at "Preparing Models" | an A100 session, 0 clips | no HF token, no retry; unproven GPU chosen | G4 is the proven GPU (R30); 429 retry on any 429; do not switch GPU without a test |
| C3 | Attempt 1 (2026-11-09 00:20): run.py was 19.7 MB; `colab exec -f` hung on this PC and the script never reached the GPU; a G4 billed for 13 minutes before anyone looked | 1.68 units | no proof the script started; script size limit unknown | R28: size under 12 MB (now 40 KB + 3 MB upload parts), proof within 180 s that `/content/out` exists, else stop |
| C4 | Attempt 2: the same hang with an 11.3 MB script | 0.57 units | the size fix was a guess, not tested | the 180 s proof caught it; chunked upload fixed it |
| C5 | Attempt 3: the G4 session was terminated 2 minutes into the install (cause unknown, probably closed in Colab Manage sessions while stopping an extra notebook); the local exec processes kept hanging | about 0.3 to 0.9 units | the owner's own browser notebook (T4) looked like ours; no clear "which session is whose" rule | the runner checks `Hardware: G4`; tell the owner which session to touch; kill local exec on every exit |
| C6 | Attempt 5: every shot failed in 10 seconds (rc=1): our H3 prompt had a blank line and Wan2GP reads a blank line as a second generation request | about 0.9 units, 15 minutes | the prompt layout was never run once on the GPU before the full batch; the proven T0 prompts had single line breaks only | builder collapses blank lines and raises if one is left; test + R30 |
| C7 | A forgotten or looping runner: the final fetch split `FILES.txt` on spaces (clip names contain spaces), tried to download "Picture", "1", "0.mp4" and ended without stopping the session (a failed fetch keeps the session on purpose) | extra billed minutes on a finished job | untested with real file names | one path per line; always check `colab sessions` after a run; stop by hand |
| C8 | Opus writer, stage 2 (Kalika): the CLI `result` kept only the last turn; the first 90% of the answer was lost | 2.62 USD | `--output-format json` joins nothing | R23: always stream-json + `join_stream`; check `num_turns` |
| C9 | Opus "repair" rewrote the 3e1 stage as 11 shots and failed validators | one Opus call, a failed stage | repair prompt let the model rewrite whole answers | targeted repair only; restore originals (kept `.bak`) |
| C10 | The Claude weekly limit was hit while Opus stages were still needed; later `h3_author --opus` and the CLI reviewers failed | blocked work for days | all heavy writer work on one subscription, no budget watch | free models (Nemotron Super, Xing) for authoring and review; `claude` limit checked before a stage |

## 3. Time and effort mistakes (images and Flow)

| # | Mistake | Root cause | Fix / rule |
|---|---|---|---|
| F1 | Keyframes accepted from reviewer verdicts and small thumbnails; at full size they had letters in the sparks (1A), a wink (1A), Brahma at the edge and cropped sages (6A, 6B), wrong crowns | the reviewer is advisory; small captures hide defects | the coordinator opens every kept picture at FULL size (R25) |
| F2 | The A and B keyframe of one shot were made as two separate generations, so they disagree (8A: Brahma standing before a flat throne; 8B: seated on a stepped dais; 2A/2B arms) and the video has to invent the change | A/B treated as "pick the better of two" instead of start and end frame of one shot | note N4: B (or A) is made as an EDIT of the other; pair review side by side; list the allowed changes |
| F3 | A long misunderstanding with the owner: "A and B are two options" versus start and end frame | not explained in the packet and the UI | R25 and the packet text: A = start, B = end, both required |
| F4 | Regenerating images with long prompts again and again (1A: 5 submits, 6A/6B: 8) when one change list on a single reference would have worked | no rule for reworks | R25: one chip, exact change list, Nano Banana Pro for reworks; do not ask for one open and one closed eye (Flow draws a wink) |
| F5 | Chip rules: the `@` picker listed OLD- tiles next to the exact name; several agents stopped, some picked the wrong one; renames "saved" silently half the time | duplicated and stale names in the project; UI quirks | exact-title rule, rename then reload and re-read; retire first; one tile per title |
| F6 | Browser tabs: the pane has a cap of about 9 tabs; finished agents left theirs open, three download agents could not start; one agent acted without `tabId` on another agent's tab and RENAMED THE WHOLE PROJECT; I closed a tab that an agent was still using | no tab discipline | R26: own tab, `tabId` on every action, close tabs of finished agents only |
| F7 | 2K download: four Haiku agents (high and low) got null captures for 20+ minutes because they clicked "More options" at x=615 instead of x=668; I found it by doing one by hand | coordinate clicks without a screenshot | recipe in `Satvik notes refer.md` and R30: find the ref or screenshot before every click |
| F8 | The Flow project was signed out in the pane; three agents started, stopped, and their lines said "done" or "blocked" without the owner knowing | no sign-in check before launching agents | check sign-in first; agents report the stop at once |
| F9 | Edit ids in my notes did not match the gallery (c989ad77, 89444d2c): an agent lost time searching | ids copied from partial notes | match tiles by exact prompt and title, not by remembered ids |
| F10 | Watermark: the detector found no sparkle in 4 of 20 images (bright cloud and gold backgrounds); and 6A carried a second, baked-in ghost star inherited from the edit reference | threshold tuned on dark images; edits copy the watermark | fixed anchor fallback (`stamps_or_anchor`); look at every corner; remove ghost stars by hand |
| F11 | The wrong GPU named in memory: a handoff note said A100, the log said G4; the owner and I argued from a wrong note | memory written from plans, not from the run log | verify from `gpu.csv` and `colab new` lines; fixed the note |

## 4. Process and my own slips

| # | Mistake | Cost | Fix / rule |
|---|---|---|---|
| P1 | Python heredocs turned `\n` inside strings into real line breaks (at least 8 times: write_pack.py, tests, build_h3_batch.py, remove_sparkle patches, NOW block paths with `\a` `\r`) | broken files caught late, wasted rounds | R20 and R30: use the Edit tool for code with backslashes; `ast.parse` after every scripted edit |
| P2 | A shell wrapper hid 2 failing Gate D tests and a push went out (ce74e37) | a bad push to fix | tests are read, not trusted through a wrapper |
| P3 | Log lines for steps that did not happen (an "applied fixes" line after a failed script; agents writing DONE lines for retired tiles) | wrong state believed | R24: a correction is a new FIX line; read the result before writing the line |
| P4 | Killing processes by a command-line pattern that also matched my own shell (twice), so the command exited 255 and the next steps did not run | lost minutes, a session left running once | kill by PID found first |
| P5 | Reviewers: the NVIDIA-hosted Nemotron Super spent every token thinking (4 empty answers even at 30000 tokens); Xing returned only thought traces; OpenRouter reviewers hit 429 when run together | hours of review time | slices of at most about 10 KB for Nemotron; run reviewers one after another; trust but triage every finding |
| P6 | The pipeline was built around the first story (Kaliya): hard-wired folders, `LEAP-*` file patterns, a style chip name identical for every story, a route name the runner rejected, no GPU path for V4 rows | two full audits found 44 HIGH gaps, closed late (R21, R22) | every story gets its own folders; one end-to-end dry run per new story |
| P7 | The sound-cue rule SX-01 (all 7 action sentences need a sound word) only showed up in the render controller after authoring: 6 of 10 shots were "not ready" | authoring ran twice (stale fields) | run `render_controller --dry-run` right after the writer, before authoring |
| P8 | "Dry run" only prints commands; nothing ever tested the real chain on one shot before the full 10-shot batch | 4 failed starts | before a full run: a one-shot run (`--ids SHOT-001`) is the first real test; look at its first clip before the rest |
| P9 | Agent briefs and agent reports were trusted too much: sign-in blocks, wrong tab, "done" lines, "I cannot open the second tile" | repeated reruns | verify what an agent says against the file, the gallery or the log; keep a short list per shot |
| P10 | Owner rules arrived mid-task (send each clip, then do not send each clip; Haiku low then high; Pro for reworks only; stop at once) and I did not always stop first | wasted calls and sends | on "stop": stop everything first, then answer; log the order in blot |

## 5. The rules that matter most (short list)

1. Prove the script started within 3 minutes of `--go` (`colab ls /content` shows `out/`), else stop the session.
2. Save every clip to the PC the minute its shot ends. Never wait for the end of the run.
3. Run ONE shot for real first; look at its clip; then the rest. A dry run is not a test.
4. Always stop the session; check `colab sessions` and `colab usage` after every run, and never touch the session that is not ours (the owner's T4 browser notebook).
5. The proven GPU is the G4. Do not change GPU, model or prompt layout without a one-shot test.
6. Prompts: single line breaks only, no blank line (Wan2GP).
7. `colab exec -f` hangs above about 7 MB on this PC: upload in 3 MB parts; run.py stays small.
8. Review the render script with ALL reviewers before `--go` (note N3), then fix, then start.
9. Keyframes: open every kept picture at full size; A/B pairs are start and end of ONE shot, check them side by side (note N4); reworks are single-reference edits.
10. Flow agents: own tab, `tabId` on every action, retire before you rename, one tile per title, screenshot before a click.
11. Code with backslashes: Edit tool, then `ast.parse`. Never a heredoc.
12. A log line is written after the result is read, not before. Corrections are new FIX lines.
13. Opus and Sonnet CLI can run out for days (weekly limit): plan authoring and reviews on the free Super model.
14. When the owner says stop, stop first.

See also: `blot.md` rules 20 to 31, `Satvik notes refer.md` (N1 to N4), `PROJECT_LOG.md` (every step), `CLAUDE.md`.

## 6. Added 2026-11-09 (later): more mistakes, found while fixing SHOT-008 and checking the script

| # | Mistake | Cost | Root cause | What a production pipeline needs |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Q1 | SHOT-008 first re-render had two black cobras with hoods rising behind Brahma from frame 48 to the end; I first called it "a dark curved shape" | a second re-render (about 1.2 units, about 30 minutes) and the owner's trust | the prompt carried the sound notes "serpents hiss softly" and "serpents shift with a faint dry hiss"; the video model draws every noun it reads | sound notes must never name a drawable thing (animals, creatures, objects not in the picture); a lint on the cues; sound described as a sound only ("a soft dry rustle") |
| Q2 | I judged the clip from 16 frames and said it looked good | wrong "all clear" given to the owner | no automatic frame check, a human glance at a sparse sample | an automatic frame scan (a vision model over every 4th frame) that lists characters, creatures, objects and arm counts and compares them with the shot script; the human check is the second line, not the first |
| Q3 | The compiled H3 prompt has grammar and content defects: "with the wind drops to a soft dry rustle" (a clause glued after "with"); the last sentence appears twice (stage 6 and 7 are identical); "non-verbal breaths at seconds 7" (broken sentence); pronoun clashes ("The figure's mouth ... his mouth ... her"); two boilerplate silence sentences repeated in every shot; curly apostrophes; jargon words "hold", "burst", "settle" that the model may take literally | unknown, probably lower clip quality in every shot | the compiler glues text pieces without a language check | prompt compiler with a grammar and duplicate check; one fixed boilerplate; no repeated sentence; no jargon in the visual part; a prompt quality gate before any render |
| Q4 | The visual part of the prompt does not say what must NOT appear (no extra people, no creatures) although the Flow job prompt did ("Show only these people and no others") | cobras, possible extra figures | the H3 layout has no negative or "only these characters" line | add the "only these characters, no creatures, no extra objects" sentence to the compiler |
| Q5 | Keyframe 8A was made without checking it against the script (Brahma seated all shot) | one full redo of 8A plus a re-render | keyframes were reviewed alone, not against the shot's own script lines | check each keyframe against the script's position and pose list |
| Q6 | The voice script was never checked for speaking speed before the render; 8 Hindi lines run 3.3 to 3.6 words a second in slots that allow 3.2 | rework of the script after the clips exist | the writer sets time windows and text separately, nothing measures the voice | the writer measures real or estimated voice length per language and loops until the line fits |
| Q7 | I never listened to or measured the audio the video model made (the aac track in every clip) | unknown: it may contain speech-like noise, music or silence | only frames were checked | measure level, silence and speech with ffmpeg and a speech detector on every clip; decide keep or replace |
| Q8 | I told the owner "the second Flow tile could not be opened" and "Brahma is seated" from agent reports before looking | wrong state reported | trusted agent text | verify against the picture before reporting |
| Q9 | The owner's words were guessed more than once (CNET, "E100", "dataset the render", "Hyde haikyu"): I answered a guess and sometimes acted on it | wasted turns | no habit of confirming an unclear order before a costly action | confirm in one line when an order is unclear and the action costs units or sends data |
| Q10 | Rules recorded without being asked (Flow wording rule) and then removed | a few minutes and noise | recorded a preference as a rule | record rules only when the owner says so |
| Q11 | Story-fidelity is not checked: the script is not compared with SOURCE.md (the audit noted it in 2026-11-08) and the writer grades itself | risk of wrong story beats in production | no independent check | an independent story-fidelity pass against the source for every reel |
| Q12 | Marathi and Hindi quality was checked only by me; the automatic easy-language checker was not run on the final lines; names like �r�"��?�r��, ��,�݅���?�� may be mispronounced by the voice model | risk of poor audio | no native review step, no pronunciation test | a short pronunciation test of the hard names with the chosen voices before generating everything; a native listener check |

See the shorter rule list in section 5. Every item here is a candidate for the production-grade pipeline checklist.

## 7. VOICES, STAGING AND FILE CHECKS (2026-11-09, found while building the voice system)
V1. LOGGED AN EDIT THAT NEVER HAPPENED: the Write of director/voice_library.py and its test was blocked by the worktree path guard, but the PROJECT_LOG line said "EDIT ... done". Check with ls (or read the result) before logging a file as written; a correction is a new FIX line.
V2. WRONG CLAIM TO THE OWNER: I said the account has no Hindi voice. The saved Granth library (canon/series/voices.json) shows eight male voices verified for BOTH Hindi and Marathi. Search the saved library BEFORE saying a voice type does not exist.
V3. REWROTE WHAT COULD BE COPIED: I started a new voice_library.py. The owner asked to copy Granth's code with minimal change. Copy source/a1_eleven.py first (job key, ledger, reuse, ffprobe, measured, export); change only plan loading, languages and paths (director/voice_cast.py, 5 offline tests).
V4. PHONE SHOWED NO AUDIO: several ElevenLabs preview files were WAV data named .mp3 (RIFF header), which a phone player shows as silent. Before sending audio check the header (ID3/mp3) with ffprobe format_name and re-encode to a real mp3 (libmp3lame 128k mono).
V5. A PREVIEW IS NOT A TEST: preview_url is the voice's own demo clip, usually not Hindi or Marathi and never our names. It says nothing about pronunciation, speed or the sacred names.
V6. PRE-FLIGHT FOUND FIVE BLOCKERS BEFORE ANY CREDIT WAS SPENT: (1) 16 of the 18 cast voices are shared-library voices not in the account, Starter has 10 voice slots; (2) Hindi Victor, Frederick, Edward are verified for hi only on eleven_multilingual_v2, not eleven_v4, so one model for all fails (v2 reads no emotion tags); (3) rate 2.0 voices (en Carter, en Matthew Schmitz, hi Frederick) may cost double; (4) 9 Hindi lines run 3.24-3.57 words per second against the 3.2 limit; (5) hard names untested. Always run the free pre-flight (account, slots, per-voice verified languages and model, rate, words per second per slot) before the first paid call.
V7. STAGING WAS NOT CHECKED AGAINST THE SCRIPTURE UNTIL AFTER THE RENDER: the Sanskrit check showed SHOT-007 should show Daksha/sages reacting and SHOT-009 should show Shiva present when Kama shoots Brahma; both rendered clips lack them (action text shows only Sandhya/Brahma and Brahma/Kamadeva). Check each shot's script against the source for omitted details BEFORE keyframes are made and say what the picture must show.
V8. DISK: the C: volume that holds Claude's temp folder reached 1 MB free (2026-11-09). Free space on C: before long jobs; never delete the owner's files to make room without telling them.
V9. WORDS-PER-SECOND DID NOT PREDICT FIT: the 3.2 w/s rule passed on paper but real clips from slow dramatic voices ran at 1.7-2.4 w/s, so 19 of 32 batch-1 clips overran their slot (up to 2.6x). Before a full paid run, generate ONE real line per voice (the hardest slot) and measure seconds against the slot; set voice speed and text length from that.
V10. A SETTING IS NOT PROVEN UNTIL ITS RESULT IS MEASURED: ElevenLabs voice_settings speed 1.15 returned clips of the same length (4.08 -> 4.16 s). Test any quality/speed knob on one cheap clip and measure before promising it as the fix; I told the owner speed + shorter text would solve it before testing.

## 8. Added 2026-11-09 (watermark and prompt review of shots 7 and 9)
W1. A TOOL THAT FINDS NO INPUT EXITS 0 AND PRINTS NOTHING: the sparkle tools only read files named *__candidate_v01.png (and need the __2K_source.jpg beside each); the v02 images matched nothing, so an earlier run "wrote nothing, rc=0" and I misread it as a tool fault. A batch tool must print how many inputs it found and fail on zero.
W2. python -I HIDES THE USER SITE-PACKAGES: cv2, scipy and torch live in AppData Roaming, so python -I raised ModuleNotFoundError. Use -I for untrusted data only, plain python for our own tools.
W3. THE AUTOMATIC DETECTOR MISSES A FAINT BIG GHOST STAR: A images of an edit carry a faint big star (inherited, F10) that the detector did not find, and the alpha-clean and lama_on_clean variants leave scratches on dark cloth and gold steps. What worked: LaMa with both stamp positions forced (small 24 at 161,161; big 48 at 56,56). Always look at the corner crop at native size for every variant; verify no change outside the window.
W4. A REVIEWER KEY EXPIRED UNSEEN: OpenRouter returned 401 (key expired) only when the review ran. Check each reviewer key with a tiny call before a review round; fall back to NVIDIA and say so.
W5. I CALLED OLD RENDERS "THE NEWEST" AND SENT THEM: the clips of shots 7 and 9 were rendered from the OLD keyframes (11-08 20:31 and 20:38) while new keyframes existed; I sent them without saying so until the owner asked. Before sending or reporting a clip, state which keyframes it was made from.
W6. TWO CODE TREES HAVE DRIFTED: anime_studio and anime_studio_merge differ (v4_to_h3.py has lattice and head-handle fixes only in merge, the batch builder only in anime_studio); a compile I ran mixed the two. Decide the live tree and sync before any code or prompt fix, else the fix is lost.
W7. KEYFRAMES WERE MADE WITHOUT CHECKING THE SHOT SCRIPT AGAIN (same as Q5, V7): 009 script says Brahma rises from the throne but both new keyframes show him seated; 007 and 009 prompts do not name the sages and Shiva who are in the pictures; 007A already shows full draw while the script starts the draw. Check pictures against per-second directives before the images are approved.
W8. A PICTURE REVIEWER IS ADVISORY AND PARTLY WRONG: Super VL said two attendants and Sandhya facing Kamadeva in 007B; the picture has three sages and Sandhya facing the viewer. Verify each picture claim at full size (F1, Q8).
W9. THE "with <cue>" GLUE IS STILL IN THE CONVERTER (v4_to_h3.py line 153, Q3): every shot prompt reads "with a veil snaps". It must be fixed once at the source, with a test, in the live tree.
W10. A FREE URL CHECK WOULD HAVE SAVED THREE PAID SESSIONS: the render setup downloads chumpy-0.71 from a GitHub release; that file answers HTTP 504 (also from this PC) while githubstatus says all operational. Before any paid session, test every external download URL of the setup from this PC with curl (free, 10 s): the requirements URLs, the model files, the git clone. Cost of not doing it today: 0.58 units, 3 sessions, about 25 minutes.
W11. THE RUNNER LOST THE ERROR TEXT: it downloads only timeline.txt and gpu.csv, not setup.log, so the first failure showed only "exit 1". Anything the setup learns must be written into timeline.txt (done: sh_retry writes the log tail) or the log must be fetched before the session stops.
W12. A BLIND RETRY IS NOT A FIX: I added a pip retry after the first 504 (right idea) but ran it before knowing the cause was persistent; the second and third attempt only confirmed it. After a failed paid start, find the cause first (free), then retry.
W13. THE OWNER'S ORDER OF WORK (2026-11-09): reel 1 first, then fix every gap. Gaps already known and parked on purpose: Hugging Face token (owner offered one), the chumpy wheel and other single downloads bundled into our upload, models cached on Drive or a private HF repo, one code tree instead of two, the converter 'with <cue>' glue, the generic mouth sentence, OpenRouter key expired. Parking them is a decision, not forgetting (blot RULE 41).
W14. P1 AGAIN (the 9th time): I rewrote part of a test file with a python heredoc and an escaped newline became a real line break; ast.parse caught it at once. For any text with a backslash use the Edit tool, never a heredoc, even for a 'small' test.
W15. A SECRET PASTED IN CHAT: the owner gave a Hugging Face token in the conversation. It is now in the chat history and in one tool call. Rule: save to secrets/ once, never echo it, send to the VM through stdin only, and ask the owner to rotate it after the job. Better habit for next time: the owner writes the file themselves.
W16. 'colab new' CAN FAIL AFTER THE SERVER CREATED THE VM: a ConnectionError (Remote end closed connection) left an unnamed G4 session billing 10 units/hour that the CLI could not stop (its state file had no record). After ANY failed 'colab new' check 'colab sessions' and 'colab usage' at once; a stray G4 must be terminated in Colab > Runtime > Manage sessions (browser signed in) or by the owner. The runner and the waiter must do this check themselves (gap, parked by blot RULE 41 but needed before the next run). Cost today: about 1.16 units and 25 minutes of attention.
W17. THE RUNNER DID NOT STOP AFTER 'ALL DONE': after the clip was home it kept downloading timeline.txt in a loop and the G4 kept billing (10 units/hour) until I stopped the session by hand about 10 minutes later. Fix before any unattended run: when RESULT.json says ALL DONE and every clip is home, fetch the logs once and stop at once.
W18. A SETUP ONLY STARTS WHEN EVERY STEP IS PROVEN ON THE REAL VM: three different failures hid behind each other (GitHub 504 for chumpy, a 'colab new' connection drop, an upload websocket drop). Each fix was found only by running; the free checks (URL, sed on the real requirements line, hash of the wheel) are what finally made attempt 7 pass.
W19. THE VOICE WINDOWS USED THE WRONG LENGTH: I sized the audio windows to the rendered CLIP (6.6 to 10.1 s) but the reel cuts each shot at its EDITORIAL length (5 to 8 s), so 14 of 54 lines ran past the cut (up to 1.46 s) and I reported "54 of 54 fit". I found it only when I read the editorial numbers before building the reel. Always get the timing basis from the assembler's own plan (timing_and_lattice.trim_in/out, editorial_duration_sec) before sizing anything; and run the downstream check (Gate D vo_fit_check) before saying "fits". Fixed: rule 42, 8 shorter lines, build_vo_tracks.py.
W20. A CHECK THAT BLOCKS IS INFORMATION, NOT AN OBSTACLE: Gate D reported script-level retention failures (narration coverage 86% vs 90%, 27 words vs 38, dead air to 1.5 s). They are real findings about the script, not about the build. Waived only by the owner's order and only those codes, written into the report; never silently.
# Pipeline audit, 2026-11-07

Scope: every part of the Anime Studio pipeline on both branches, what each part does, what is done, what is tested, what is not built, and what is risky.
Method: file inventory of both branches (`git ls-tree`), a dry-run merge, all test suites re-run, the spec's acceptance checks re-run on real files, test-to-module cross-reference. No model call, no render, no story file was touched. Everything below was observed in this session unless marked "not verified".

## 1. Verdict in ten lines

1. The code for the whole path exists and is tested, but it sits on **two branches that have never been merged**: `v4-architecture-2026-11-07` (writer, validator, H3 compile/lint/route, Gate D audio, UI wizard: 17 commits, 196 files) and `universal-v1.1` (colour, retention, flash, captions, post.py: 24 commits, 86 files). A dry-run merge gives **4 conflicted files, 8 hunks** (`README.md`, `STATUS.md`, `director/write_pack.py`, `h3/render_controller.py`). It is small and mechanical, but until it is done no single checkout runs the whole path.
2. **Universal branch (the colour/retention/post layer): complete against the spec.** WP0-WP9, amendments A1-A28 and the caption components 9.1-9.8 are built; core 387 tests (+1 release gate that is skipped on purpose), director 488, h3 178; flow and ui show only the failures that already existed on main.
3. **V4 branch: complete as code, with three named holes** (section 6): the Step 9 QC runner, the Gate D assembly runner, and the live author run are not built; the pre-render controller has no GPU backend wired.
4. **Nothing has been rendered for production.** The only real video work is the 2026-11-06 T0 test (8 clips of one scene, on Colab). `post.py` has run only on synthetic clips.
5. **No story has gone through the finished pipeline.** The real Kaliya pack does not exist in the new form (the old T0 shots have no `look` block, so 8 of 8 fail P2).
6. **Two caption engines exist:** the new one in `core/` (universal) and the older one inside `h3/gate_d_audio.py` (V4). They must be unified at the merge.
7. **The style packs are structurally complete but not measured:** no plate has a measured Lab value, no LUT file exists, `braj_earth` has no grade numbers, `gates.sat_avg_ceiling` is still null, and the gate limits are untuned starting values.
8. The free reviewers (Super VL, Dots) were run on every changed area; Dots is unreliable on long inputs (empty answers), so some batches were covered by Super VL only.
9. Fonts are now committed to git (four SIL OFL families, 2.9 MB). The spec said "no fonts staged"; this was a deliberate change after you supplied them. Licences are kept beside the files.
10. Nothing under `granthstudio` was touched (checked by file times). No key, image, clip or model weight is tracked (secret scan clean, no file over 1 MB).

## 2. The pipeline, stage by stage

| # | Stage | What it does | Where it lives | Tests | State |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | Story intake | A YouTube link or pasted text becomes `SOURCE.md`; ASR fallback when a video has no captions | `director/yt_transcript.py`, `asr_transcribe.py` (both branches) | yes (no network in tests) | done |
| 1 | Writer | Story text becomes a production pack (`PACK.md`, `shots.json`, bible) through five gates; three model paths, free models by default; v2.3 prompt is now the staged default | `director/write_pack.py`, `writer_prompts.py` (V4), `MASTER_PROMPT_v2.3.md` | yes, 16 test files touch `write_pack` | code done; **no live v2.3 or V4 writer run on a real story in this session** (model call needs your go) |
| 2 | Pack checks (V4) | Validates every stage of the writer output: schema, voices, languages, simple-language rule, retries and fallback for free models | `director/pack_validator.py`, `simple_language.py`, `retry_policy.py`, `run_registry.py` | yes | done |
| 3 | Pack checks (universal) | P0-P13 rules (palette, look block, flash, fonts...), R1-R10 retention rules, timeline builder; `check_pack.py --strict` | `core/pack_rules.py`, `retention_rules.py`, `timeline.py`, `director/check_pack.py` | yes (59 + 34 + 24 + fixtures) | done |
| 4 | Style packs | The look as data: palettes, acts, phases, grades, typography, flash colours | `styles/braj_earth.json`, `deva_neon.json`, `core/style_pack.py`, converters in `tools/` | yes | structure done; **values not measured** (section 6) |
| 5 | Flow images | Builds image jobs from a pack, files downloaded 2K images, removes the corner sparkle, reviews candidates, G1 palette gate | `flow/scripts/*` | yes (flow 130 pass) | code done; the image generation itself is a manual browser step in Flow, not code |
| 6 | H3 prep (V4) | V4 pack becomes an H3 story, 5-mode router, prompt compiler, linter, asset manifest, fallback ladder, voice engine | `h3/v4_to_h3.py`, `router.py`, `compile_h3_sing8.py`, `schema_and_linter.py`, `asset_manifest.py`, `fallback_policy.py`, `voice_engine.py` | yes (h3 595) | done |
| 7 | Pre-render controller | Lints, compiles, writes prompts, workflows and the assembly script per shot; blocks on any error | `h3/render_controller.py` | yes | done as "prepare only"; **no GPU backend wired** |
| 8 | Render | The H3 model makes video and audio per shot, on Colab or Kaggle | `director/run_kaggle.py`, Colab CLI (research notes) | run_kaggle tested | **not part of the controller; T0 test only, no production render** |
| 9 | Clip QA | Frame sheet, luma flicker, drift, saturation, loudness, flash F1/F2, colour criteria and colour-blind panel | `director/clip_tools.py` (`gates`), `visual_qa.py`, `core/flash_check.py`, `frame_metrics.py`, `cvd.py` | yes | done |
| 10 | Step 9 QC (V4) | Final review gate: SFX, continuity, closing payoff, labels | `h3/step9_qc.py` | yes | functions done; **runner not built** |
| 11 | Audio plan (V4) | Per-language voice files, BGM presence, VO fit, post-AAC loudness, its own `.ass` captions | `h3/gate_d_audio.py`, `voice_manifest.py` | yes | plan code done; **assembly runner not built; ElevenLabs needs your go** |
| 12 | Assembly | ffmpeg plan with BT.709 delivery flags, loudness pass-through, G3 colour seams | `h3/assemble_reel.py` | yes | done (plans only, it never runs ffmpeg) |
| 13 | Post | Shot match, act grade, impacts, one 16-bit-to-8-bit conversion, captions, encode, final gates, refuse on FAIL, `colour_report.json`, SRT/WebVTT sidecars | `director/post.py` | 17 tests on synthetic episodes | done; **never run on real clips** |
| 14 | Analytics | Maps retention-graph dips to shots | `core/retention_report.py` | yes (24) | tool done; no analytics file exists yet |
| 15 | UI wizard (V4) | Local control panel: Story, Analysis, Gates A-D, Images, Render, Export | `ui/server.py`, `ui/pipeline.py`, `ui/static/` | yes (ui 253) + browser check at phone and desktop width | done; **not verified:** how it will display the new rule results (`rules` list from the universal `check_pack`) once the branches are merged |

## 3. Part by part: what each module is

### 3.1 `core/` (universal branch, 13 modules, 3,829 lines, 387 tests)
- `style_pack.py`: loads `core.json` and style packs; CIEDE2000, sRGB to Lab, WCAG contrast, pack validation.
- `core.json`: every tunable number (delivery flags, flash limits, retention windows, gate limits, safe zones). Safe zone default is now your Reels decision (top 14%, bottom 35%, caption band 50-65%); `safe_zone_templates` holds reels, shorts and youtube.
- `timeline.py`: turns shots into episodes with frame-exact timing; reports episode-length problems.
- `pack_rules.py`: rules P0-P13 (malformed input is a P0 FAIL, never a traceback).
- `retention_rules.py`: R1-R10 (cold open, motion by 0.5 s, face change, hook caption, no hold in the first 3 s, change cadence, re-hook, end loop, sound from frame 0).
- `frame_metrics.py`: ffmpeg signalstats and Pillow frame statistics.
- `flash_check.py`: F1 (more than 3 flashes in one second refuses) and F2 (red flash warns). Odd transitions count as a flash (owner-confirmed).
- `lut.py`: LUT maths: shot match (clamped), act grade, `.cube` read and write.
- `cvd.py`: deuteranopia simulation for the colour-blind panel.
- `captions.py`: builds the `.ass` file: safe band, lockup, contrast, minimum on-screen time, measured two-line wrapping, glyph check, hook-word emphasis, karaoke with phrase fallback, mixed-script fonts, platform templates.
- `caption_text.py`: grapheme clusters (Devanagari conjuncts), script runs, a pure-Python font cmap reader, glyph coverage, measured wrapping, mixed-script font markup.
- `caption_export.py`: SRT and WebVTT, ElevenLabs alignment parser (no API call), karaoke text, contact-sheet plan (argv only), frame hashing, ffmpeg libass/HarfBuzz preflight.
- `retention_report.py`: dip-to-shot mapping from an analytics file.

### 3.2 `director/` (both branches; universal 17 modules, V4 23 modules)
- Writer and prompts: `write_pack.py`, `writer_prompts.py` (V4), `style_bible.py`, `acting_library.py`, `shot_schema.py` (look block validation in universal).
- Checks: `check_pack.py` (universal version runs the P and R rules; the V4 version is the old 43-line one), `layout_validator.py`, `pack_validator.py`, `simple_language.py`, `retry_policy.py`.
- Registry and state: `run_registry.py`, `backfill_registry.py`, `story_state.py`, `story_links.py`, `ops_checks.py` (disk, server freshness, Colab guard).
- Render side: `h3_director.py`, `dry_run.py`, `run_kaggle.py`, `t0_variants.py`.
- Clip side: `clip_tools.py` (QA sheet, loudness, `gates`), `visual_qa.py`.
- Post: `post.py` (universal only, 600 lines).

### 3.3 `h3/` (V4 17 modules; universal has the older 6)
Router, compiler, linter, render controller, asset manifest, fallback ladder (4 rungs), Step 9 QC functions, voice engine, voice manifest, Gate D audio, V4-to-H3 converter, author step, pipeline contract (the ten ordered steps the UI shows), free-model end-to-end sample.

### 3.4 `flow/scripts/` (18 files)
Job builder, pack-to-spec, download queue and filer, sparkle removal (LaMa), neighbour and review sheets, reviewer of candidates, bridge from a Flow keyframe to the video size, the free-model coder and reviewer helpers (`dots_coder.py`, `dots_review.py`), and the new G1 `palette_check.py`.

### 3.5 `tools/` (universal 7 + V4 2)
`convert_bible.py`, `convert_deva_bible.py`, `convert_deva_shots.py` (flat and H3 mode), `lint_pack.py`, `make_lut.py`, `measure_plate.py`, `calibrate_sat_ceiling.py` (universal); `secret_scan.py` and `auto_log.py` (V4).

### 3.6 `ui/`
`server.py` (1,905 lines, local API on 127.0.0.1) and `pipeline.py` plus static JS. The JS has no unit tests (syntax check and a manual browser check only).

## 4. Spec acceptance (section 6.3), re-run today

| Check | Result |
|---|---|
| All suites pass, counts before and after | Before (spec baseline): director 385, h3 159, flow 114, ui 161. After: core 387 (+1 skipped release gate), director 488, h3 178, flow 130 pass + 2 failures, ui 161 pass + 1 failure. The 3 failures are the same real-pack tests that fail on main: they need a local, untracked pack folder. |
| check_pack on Kaliya with story.json: no P1, P2, P4 FAIL for Krishna | The real new pack does not exist. On the old T0 shots: 8 P2 FAIL (no look block), 1 R1 FAIL, 8 R6 FAIL (5.17 s static gaps), no P1 or P4 FAIL. All are real content problems of the old shots. |
| DEVA template + Shiva story: only P5 FAILs on SHOT-02 | pass (test `test_deva_template_after_convert_gives_only_the_known_p5_fails`); P10 now passes because fonts exist |
| WP4 regression fixtures | pass (28 tests across `test_check_pack_rules.py` and `test_post.py` re-run) |
| post.py on a synthetic episode: yuv420p, bt709 x3, tv, `colour_report.json`, `loudness.json`; injected 4-flash second refuses | pass |
| `lint_pack.py deva_neon` lists Hanuman, Karna, Durga gaps | pass (also lists Shiva, found by the role rule) |
| OPEN_QUESTIONS.md exists | yes; all eight questions closed with the recommended defaults |
| Nothing under granthstudio; no images, clips, keys staged | pass for images, clips, keys; **fonts are staged** (see verdict 9) |
| README and STATUS updated; each WP one commit; not pushed until your go | updated; WP commits exist (some WPs are split into parts); pushed after your approval |

## 5. How much is tested

Every module on both branches is referenced by at least one test file. Counts today: universal 1,348 tests across the five suites (1,344 pass, 3 known data-dependent failures, 1 release gate skipped on purpose); V4 1,627 (director 663, h3 595, ui 253, flow 116, all pass). Seven review rounds by two free reviewers each found real defects that were fixed with tests; the last rounds found only low-severity ones (round 7: three small calibration-tool defects, plus one contact-sheet bug found by a real libass render, not by a reviewer).

## 6. What is NOT done, ranked by impact

1. **Merge the two branches.** 4 conflicts, 8 hunks. After the merge: run all suites, wire the universal gates into the UI, and replace Gate D's own caption code with `core/captions.py` and `caption_export.py` so there is one caption engine.
2. **No production render and no real post.py run.** Needed to tune the limits (G1/G2 dE 6, G3 dE 8, static 3.5/4.0 s) and to check LUTs on real frames.
3. **Style packs are unmeasured.** No `measured` plate values (G1 is skipped with a warning), no LUT files (`styles/luts` does not exist; post.py falls back to the pack's grade numbers), `braj_earth` has no grade numbers at all (Kaliya would export ungraded), `gates.sat_avg_ceiling` is null (G2 uses a provisional 181.02 with a warning). Tools exist for all of it (`measure_plate`, `make_lut`, `calibrate_sat_ceiling`); they need approved plates and reference frames.
4. **V4 runners not built:** Step 9 QC runner, Gate D assembly runner, live author run. The functions behind them exist and are tested.
5. **Render backend not wired** into the controller.
6. **Paid ElevenLabs:** parser and karaoke path exist; the API shape is from public documentation and unverified; any live use needs your go.
7. **Story work:** the writer run, caption text and hook words, Kaliya defects, Mahadev fourth reel. Not started, by your instruction.
8. **Manual checks from spec 6.4:** approve LUTs on 3 stills per act, review one episode on a D65 monitor and two phones, check caption placement against the platform overlays, run DEVA's publish gate.

## 7. Known limits and risks

- Caption widths are measured with Pillow basic layout (no libraqm here): Devanagari conjunct widths can be slightly over-estimated, so line breaks may differ a little from the real render. A real libass render of Marathi conjunct text looked correct (HarfBuzz shaper active).
- Caption size defaults (34 px at 1080 wide, outline 8%) are tune values; the shorts and youtube safe zones are tune values.
- Free reviewers: Dots returns empty answers on long inputs; Super VL occasionally cites code it was not shown. Every finding was checked by hand against the code before acting.
- The automatic log hook is installed but was not seen firing in this session (needs a new session).
- Stale docs on the V4 branch: its `STATUS.md` still shows the older suite counts.
- Two review claims were rejected as by design (karaoke gap handling, caption centre shifted away from the right button rail); both are documented in `research/TRIAGE_R7_2026-11-07.md`.

## 8. Suggested next steps

1. Merge the branches (one session, then all suites, then a free review round on the merged files).
2. Start the actual story; the pipeline is ready for it. Order: writer run (your go), caption text and hook words, approved plates (`measure_plate`), first render of one episode, then `calibrate_sat_ceiling` and limit tuning.
3. Build the three V4 runners and wire the controller to the render backend.
