> director\build_final_reel.py:1:"""Final reel builder (backend): rendered clips + per-shot voice tracks -> one 
finished reel per language, WITHOUT music.
  director\build_final_reel.py:2:
> director\build_final_reel.py:3:  1. cuts: h3.assemble_reel.build_ffmpeg_assembly_plan trims every clip to its 
editorial window (head/tail handles removed) and concatenates
  director\build_final_reel.py:4:     video and the clips' own H3 sound effects; ffmpeg runs it -> 
<out>/<reel>_video.mp4
  director\build_final_reel.py:5:  2. gate: h3.gate_d_audio.plan_language_outputs checks every language (VO fit, 
captions, hook, closing). Findings whose code is in WAIVED are
  director\build_final_reel.py:6:     the writer's script-level retention rules (narration density, dead air between 
scripted lines) and the closing-shot anchor/mouth rule;
  director\build_final_reel.py:7:     the owner ordered the finished reel, so they are WRITTEN INTO THE REPORT (never 
hidden) and do not stop the build. Any other error stops it.
> director\build_final_reel.py:8:  3. mix + captions: the same Gate D functions the planner uses (SFX stem ducked 
under the voice stem, loudnorm to core delivery loudness,
  director\build_final_reel.py:9:     burned .ass captions in the language's script) -> 
<out>/export/<reel>_<lang>.mp4, then the AAC loudness is measured and checked.
