W10. A FREE URL CHECK WOULD HAVE SAVED THREE PAID SESSIONS: the render setup downloads chumpy-0.71 from a GitHub release; that file answers HTTP 504 (also from this PC) while githubstatus says all operational. Before any paid session, test every external download URL of the setup from this PC with curl (free, 10 s): the requirements URLs, the model files, the git clone. Cost of not doing it today: 0.58 units, 3 sessions, about 25 minutes.
W11. THE RUNNER LOST THE ERROR TEXT: it downloads only timeline.txt and gpu.csv, not setup.log, so the first failure showed only "exit 1". Anything the setup learns must be written into timeline.txt (done: sh_retry writes the log tail) or the log must be fetched before the session stops.
W12. A BLIND RETRY IS NOT A FIX: I added a pip retry after the first 504 (right idea) but ran it before knowing the cause was persistent; the second and third attempt only confirmed it. After a failed paid start, find the cause first (free), then retry.
W13. THE OWNER'S ORDER OF WORK (2026-11-09): reel 1 first, then fix every gap. Gaps already known and parked on purpose: Hugging Face token (owner offered one), the chumpy wheel and other single downloads bundled into our upload, models cached on Drive or a private HF repo, one code tree instead of two, the converter 'with <cue>' glue, the generic mouth sentence, OpenRouter key expired. Parking them is a decision, not forgetting (blot RULE 41).
W14. P1 AGAIN (the 9th time): I rewrote part of a test file with a python heredoc and an escaped newline became a real line break; ast.parse caught it at once. For any text with a backslash use the Edit tool, never a heredoc, even for a 'small' test.
W15. A SECRET PASTED IN CHAT: the owner gave a Hugging Face token in the conversation. It is now in the chat history and in one tool call. Rule: save to secrets/ once, never echo it, send to the VM through stdin only, and ask the owner to rotate it after the job. Better habit for next time: the owner writes the file themselves.
W16. 'colab new' CAN FAIL AFTER THE SERVER CREATED THE VM: a ConnectionError (Remote end closed connection) left an unnamed G4 session billing 10 units/hour that the CLI could not stop (its state file had no record). After ANY failed 'colab new' check 'colab sessions' and 'colab usage' at once; a stray G4 must be terminated in Colab > Runtime > Manage sessions (browser signed in) or by the owner. The runner and the waiter must do this check themselves (gap, parked by blot RULE 41 but needed before the next run). Cost today: about 1.16 units and 25 minutes of attention.
W17. THE RUNNER DID NOT STOP AFTER 'ALL DONE': after the clip was home it kept downloading timeline.txt in a loop and the G4 kept billing (10 units/hour) until I stopped the session by hand about 10 minutes later. Fix before any unattended run: when RESULT.json says ALL DONE and every clip is home, fetch the logs once and stop at once.
W18. A SETUP ONLY STARTS WHEN EVERY STEP IS PROVEN ON THE REAL VM: three different failures hid behind each other (GitHub 504 for chumpy, a 'colab new' connection drop, an upload websocket drop). Each fix was found only by running; the free checks (URL, sed on the real requirements line, hash of the wheel) are what finally made attempt 7 pass.
W19. THE VOICE WINDOWS USED THE WRONG LENGTH: I sized the audio windows to the rendered CLIP (6.6 to 10.1 s) but the reel cuts each shot at its EDITORIAL length (5 to 8 s), so 14 of 54 lines ran past the cut (up to 1.46 s) and I reported "54 of 54 fit". I found it only when I read the editorial numbers before building the reel. Always get the timing basis from the assembler's own plan (timing_and_lattice.trim_in/out, editorial_duration_sec) before sizing anything; and run the downstream check (Gate D vo_fit_check) before saying "fits". Fixed: rule 42, 8 shorter lines, build_vo_tracks.py.
W20. A CHECK THAT BLOCKS IS INFORMATION, NOT AN OBSTACLE: Gate D reported script-level retention failures (narration coverage 86% vs 90%, 27 words vs 38, dead air to 1.5 s). They are real findings about the script, not about the build. Waived only by the owner's order and only those codes, written into the report; never silently.
# Voice system for the anime pipeline (design for review), 2026-11-09

Owner orders: copy the GranthStudio ElevenLabs "fix the character voice" system; NO regeneration (every line is generated once); every step reconfirmed with the reviewers with all possibilities listed; do not waste ElevenLabs credits. Nothing below has been generated or spent yet.

## 1. What GranthStudio does (read from its code, read-only)
Files: `scripts/pipeline/voice_library.py`, `scripts/source/a1_eleven.py`, `canon/series/voices.json`, `canon/audio/A1_eleven_voices.json`, `canon/audio/A1_eleven_measured.json`, `canon/adhyay_01/audio_freeze.json`.
1. **Voice library** (`voices.json`): the account's voices fetched once from the API and normalised: voice_id, name, gender, age, accent, descriptive, use_case, hindi_verified, marathi_verified (from `verified_languages`), status ASSIGNED / AVAILABLE / MISSING_FROM_ACCOUNT, assigned_to, owner_note.
2. **Voice map** (`A1_eleven_voices.json`): `{"mr": {"narrator": voice_id, ...}, "hi": {...}}`. ONE fixed voice id per character per language, never changed.
3. **Job key** = sha256(language | voice id | model | settings | text). The clip file is named after the key. A re-run with the same key reuses the accepted clip; a changed text, voice, model or setting makes a NEW clip and never overwrites an accepted one. So a re-run buys nothing twice.
4. **Credit ledger**: append-only, file-locked; reserves the estimate BEFORE each call, settles with the API's own `character-cost` header; refuses past the cap (default 8,000 credits) or while any reservation is open.
5. **Gate to spend**: `jobs` (dry list with credit estimate) is free; `run` needs `--allow-paid` and a cap.
6. **Measure**: every accepted clip is probed with ffprobe (real duration); a file that cannot be decoded or has an implausible duration stops the run. The measured file feeds the timing plan: every line's window must be at least its measured seconds.
7. **Freeze file**: sha256 of the plan, the measured file, the script text, and the manifest; "voices NOT VALIDATED until the owner has listened".
8. **Export**: accepted clips decoded to mono 16-bit wav named `<line>.<lang>.wav` for the mix.

## 2. What we already have in this project
- `bible.json` has `voice_map` = {NARRATOR, CHAR-KALI, CHAR-MARKANDEYA, CHAR-HIMALAYAN-MUNIS, CHAR-BRAHMA, CHAR-SAVITRI, CHAR-DAKSHA, CHAR-MANASA-PUTRAS, ... } each with en, hi, mr = placeholder ids (`placeholder-NARRATOR-hi`). `h3/voice_engine.py` and `h3/voice_manifest.py` define the rules (VM-*: one fixed voice id per character per language) and a manifest of wavs; nothing calls ElevenLabs. Gate D (`h3/gate_d_audio.py`) mixes the wavs, `vo_fit` checks length against the slot.
- Reel 1 script: 18 lines per language (10 narration + 8 dialogue), speakers NARRATOR, HIMALAYAN-MUNIS, MARKANDEYA, KAMADEVA, BRAHMA, SHIVA. 2,496 characters in all (en 850, hi 803, mr 843). Account: Starter, 35,704 credits left.
- ElevenLabs account voices: English premade (George, Brian, Adam, Bill, Daniel, ...), Marathi professional (Bipin narrator, Sharad deep powerful narrator, Kalyani, Radha K, Shrey, Tukaram x2, Ativir, Swapnil J, Vinayak, others). NO Hindi voice in the account. Shared library (free to add on Starter, 10 slots): Hindi narrators such as Ayush M (deep mythology narrator), Ritu Rathore (soulful female), Natraj, Ajay, Ibad, Azad.
- Models (from the API, cost multiplier per character): eleven_v4 x1.0, eleven_v3 x1.0, eleven_v4_turbo x0.5, eleven_v3_conversational x0.5; all support hi and mr; eleven_multilingual_v2, flash_v2_5, turbo_v2_5 support hi but NOT mr.

## 3. Proposed design for us (copy of the Granth system, adapted)
New files (no change to existing ones except filling the voice_map):
- `director/voice_library.py`: fetch + normalise + write `<story>/voices_library.json` (read-only API calls, free) including each voice's free `preview_url`.
- `<story pack>/voices_cast.json`: the voice map, filled by the owner's choice after listening to free previews; MUST resolve every speaker x language of the script.
- `director/voice_cast.py`: `jobs` (free dry list), `run` (paid, `--allow-paid --cap N`), `measured`, `export`, with the job key, the ledger, reuse, ffprobe checks and the manifest, exactly as in Granth, reading `narration_by_lang` and `dialogue_by_lang` of the pack's shots.json.
- Pre-flight checks before any spend: every speaker has a cast voice in each language; the voice is `hindi_verified`/`marathi_verified` for that language or the owner accepted it; text passes the easy-language and the words-per-second check; a hard-name list is tested first; total credits vs the cap.
- Tests offline with a fake HTTP (no API calls).

## 4. Decisions with ALL possibilities (reviewers: argue each)
D1 **Model**: (a) eleven_v4 x1.0 (newest, best claim for hi/mr); (b) eleven_v4_turbo x0.5 (half the cost, quality unknown); (c) eleven_v3 x1.0; (d) eleven_v3_conversational x0.5; (e) multilingual_v2 for Hindi only (cheaper, not Marathi). Risk: quality for Marathi/Hindi and sacred names is untested on this account.
D2 **Voices per language**: (a) 1 voice for everyone; (b) narrator + 1 male + 1 female (3); (c) one voice per character (6 speakers x 3 languages = 18 voices; account slot limit 10 for added library voices, premade/Marathi pro voices already in account do not use slots). Consistency rule VM-*: same speaker keeps the same voice in every shot and reel.
D3 **Test before the full run**: (a) none (no); (b) 3 short lines per language incl. hard names (about 360 credits, 1%); (c) full run directly. Free previews first (voice `preview_url` samples cost 0 credits) so voices are chosen by ear before any paid call.
D4 **Timing fit without regeneration**: (a) generate once then fit with ffmpeg `atempo` (free, up to about 8% without artefacts); (b) regenerate with speed setting (costs credits); (c) shorten text (changes meaning, parity across languages); (d) widen the slot using spare clip frames (30 to 43 per shot); (e) shorten text BEFORE generation only for lines that the words-per-second rule already marks too fast (8 Hindi lines).
D5 **Pronunciation**: (a) trust the model; (b) test the hard names with 2 candidate spellings first (�r�"��?�r��, ��,�݅���?��, �݅��?��, ����?���1��?�r�_, �r�_����?��,����؅_; Marathi forms); (c) use a pronunciation dictionary/IPA if the API offers it (cost 0); decide after the test.
D6 **Voice settings**: default vs fixed (stability/similarity/style/speed) saved IN the job key so they can never drift; changing them = a new key = paid. Choose once, before the run.
D7 **Continuity inside a shot**: send previous_text/next_text for lines of the same shot so intonation joins (no extra cost) vs independent lines.
D8 **Where the clip files live**: local D: only (small mp3s, 2,496 characters is about 3 to 4 minutes of audio).
D9 **Mouths are closed in every clip**: dialogue is voice-over; keep, or add lip-sync later (out of scope).
D10 **Spend control**: cap per run (proposal 3,000 credits for the full reel, 400 for the test); the run refuses to start if the estimate exceeds the cap or any reservation is open; every clip's real cost is read from the API header.
D11 **Order of work (each step reviewed)**: S1 library + free previews (no spend) -> owner picks voices -> S2 cast file + lint (no spend) -> S3 code + tests -> S4 `jobs` dry run -> S5 test run 360 credits (owner listens) -> S6 full run once -> S7 measure + fit + wavs -> S8 freeze file.

## 5. What would make us regenerate (to prevent)
Wrong text (fix the 8 Hindi lines and wording BEFORE), wrong voice (choose by free preview), wrong model (test first), a name said wrongly (test first), a line too long for its slot (fit locally), a changed setting (frozen in the key), a crash mid-run (ledger + reuse by key), a duplicate call (reservation lock).
"""Ordered H3 pipeline plan (pure, no I/O). The UI shows it; render_controller.plan_pipeline fills the results.

A step result is {"ok": bool, "reasons": [str], "details": {...}}. A missing result = pending.
Assembly is allowed only when every PRE_ASSEMBLY step is ready. The loudness check runs after the AAC export,
so it never blocks assembly.
"""

from h3.shot_table_spec import LOUDNESS

STEP_ORDER = (
    ("lint", "Lint the shot rows (linter, profile, paths)"),
    ("route", "Route each shot to an H3 mode (5-mode router)"),
    ("prompt", "Compile each shot prompt"),
    ("manifest", "Asset manifest: hashes current, no missing or placeholder clips"),
    ("fallback", "Fallback ladder: no shot waits at the human gate"),
    ("render", "H3 render results exist for every shot"),
    ("step9_qc", "Step 9 final QC (SFX, continuity, closing payoff, labels)"),
    ("gate_d", "Gate D audio plan for every selected language"),
    ("assembly", "Assembly (one reel per language)"),
    ("loudness", f"Post-AAC loudness check ({LOUDNESS['target_lufs']:g} LUFS, TP <= {LOUDNESS['tp_ceiling_dbtp']:g} dBTP)"),
)
PRE_ASSEMBLY = ("lint", "route", "prompt", "manifest", "fallback", "render", "step9_qc", "gate_d")
POST_ASSEMBLY = ("loudness",)
READY, BLOCKED, PENDING = "ready", "blocked", "pending"


def _step(sid, label, status, reasons, details=None):
    return {"id": sid, "label": label, "status": status, "reasons": list(reasons), "details": dict(details or {})}


def build_plan(results):
    """results: {step_id: {"ok": bool, "reasons": [...], "details": {...}}}. Returns the ordered list of steps."""
    unknown = set(results) - {sid for sid, _ in STEP_ORDER}
    if unknown:
        raise ValueError(f"unknown pipeline step(s): {sorted(unknown)}")
    steps, status = [], {}
    for sid, label in STEP_ORDER:
        if sid == "assembly":
            blockers = [s for s in PRE_ASSEMBLY if status[s] == BLOCKED]
            waits = [s for s in PRE_ASSEMBLY if status[s] == PENDING]
            if blockers:
                st, reasons = BLOCKED, [f"{s}: {r}" for s in blockers for r in steps_reasons(steps, s)]
            elif waits:
                st, reasons = PENDING, [f"waits for {s}" for s in waits]
            else:
                st, reasons = READY, []
            steps.append(_step(sid, label, st, reasons))
            status[sid] = st
            continue
        res = results.get(sid)
        if res is None:
            st, reasons, details = PENDING, [f"not run yet"], {}
        else:
            details = res.get("details", {})
            if res.get("ok"):
                st, reasons = READY, []
            else:
                st, reasons = BLOCKED, list(res.get("reasons") or ["failed without a reason"])
        steps.append(_step(sid, label, st, reasons, details))
        status[sid] = st
    return steps


def steps_reasons(steps, sid):
    return next(s["reasons"] for s in steps if s["id"] == sid)


def assembly_allowed(steps):
    """True only when the assembly step is ready (all PRE_ASSEMBLY gates passed)."""
    return any(s["id"] == "assembly" and s["status"] == READY for s in steps)
            if not vid:
                raise SystemExit(f"no voice id for {lang}/{l['voice']} in the voice map")
            text = voices.prep_text(l[lang])
            mdl = ((models or {}).get(lang) or {}).get(l["voice"], model)
            spd = (line_speed or {}).get(f"{i}.{lang}")
            st = {"speed": spd} if spd else dict(SETTINGS)                           # speed is part of the job key: a new speed is a NEW clip, an old accepted clip is never overwritten
            jobs.append({"id": f"{i}.{lang}", "line": i, "lang": lang, "voice": l["voice"], "voice_id": vid, "model": mdl, "text": text,
                         "text_sha256": hashlib.sha256(text.encode("utf-8")).hexdigest(), "credits": len(text), "settings": st, "key": job_key(lang, vid, mdl, text, st)})
    return jobs


class Ledger:
    """Append-only credit ledger: reserve the estimate BEFORE a call (under a file lock, so two processes cannot both pass the cap), settle after;
    refuses past the cap or while any reservation is open. `confirmed` = the cost came from the API's own report, not from our estimate."""
    def __init__(self, path: Path, cap: int):
        self.path, self.cap = path, cap

    def rows(self) -> dict:
        out = {}
        if self.path.exists():
            for ln in self.path.read_text(encoding="utf-8").splitlines():
                r = json.loads(ln)
                out[r["id"]] = r
        return out

    def committed(self) -> int:
        return sum(r["credits"] for r in self.rows().values())

    def unconfirmed(self) -> int:
        return sum(1 for r in self.rows().values() if r["state"] == "SETTLED" and not r.get("confirmed"))

    def _add(self, r: dict):
        self.path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        with open(self.path, "a", encoding="utf-8") as f:
            f.write(json.dumps(r) + "\n")

    def _lock(self):
        lock = self.path.with_suffix(".lock")
        lock.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        for _ in range(100):
            try:
                return os.open(str(lock), os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_RDWR), lock
            except FileExistsError:
                try:
                    if time.time() - lock.stat().st_mtime > 60:                  # a crashed process left it behind
                        lock.unlink(missing_ok=True)
                except FileNotFoundError:
                    pass
                time.sleep(0.1)
        raise SystemExit("the credit ledger is locked by another run")

    def reserve(self, jid: str, credits: int):
        fd, lock = self._lock()
        try:
            if any(r["state"] == "RESERVED" for r in self.rows().values()):
                raise SystemExit("an earlier reservation is still open: check the ElevenLabs usage page, then settle it by hand")
            if self.committed() + credits > self.cap:
                raise SystemExit(f"credit cap {self.cap} would be exceeded ({self.committed()} used + {credits})")
            self._add({"id": jid, "state": "RESERVED", "credits": credits, "t": time.time()})
        finally:
            os.close(fd)
            lock.unlink(missing_ok=True)

    def settle(self, jid: str, credits: int, confirmed: bool):
        self._add({"id": jid, "state": "SETTLED", "credits": credits, "confirmed": confirmed, "t": time.time()})


def http(method: str, path: str, key: str, body: dict | None = None, timeout: int = 120):
    req = urllib.request.Request(API + path, method=method, data=None if body is None else json.dumps(body).encode(),
                                 headers={"xi-api-key": key, "Content-Type": "application/json", "Accept": "*/*"})
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as r:
            return r.read(), dict(r.headers)
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
        raise RuntimeError(f"HTTP {e.code}: {e.read()[:200].decode('utf-8', 'ignore')}") from None


def probe_seconds(path: Path) -> float:
    """Decoded duration of the clip (ffprobe); an undecodable file raises."""
    out = subprocess.run(["ffprobe", "-v", "error", "-show_entries", "format=duration", "-of", "csv=p=0", str(path)], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)
    if out.returncode != 0 or not out.stdout.strip():
        raise RuntimeError(f"the audio does not decode: {out.stderr.strip()[:120]}")
    return float(out.stdout.strip())


def sha256_file(p: Path) -> str:
    return hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()


def _save(man: dict, path: Path):
    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    tmp = path.with_suffix(".tmp")
    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(man, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1), encoding="utf-8")
    os.replace(tmp, path)


def run(jobs: list, out: Path, cap: int, key: str, post=http, ledger: Ledger | None = None, probe=probe_seconds) -> dict:
    led = ledger or Ledger(LEDGER, cap)
    mpath = out / "eleven_manifest.json"
    prev = json.loads(mpath.read_text(encoding="utf-8")) if mpath.exists() else {"lines": []}
    rows = {r["key"]: r for r in prev["lines"] if r.get("ok") and r.get("key") and (out / r["file"]).exists() and sha256_file(out / r["file"]) == r["mp3_sha256"]}      # accepted clips are reused, never re-bought
    reused = 0
    failed = None
    for j in jobs:
        if j["key"] in rows:
            reused += 1
            continue
        row = {k: j[k] for k in ("id", "line", "lang", "voice", "voice_id", "model", "text", "text_sha256", "key", "settings")}
        f = out / "mp3" / j["lang"] / f"{j['id']}.{j['key'][:10]}.mp3"
        jid = f"{j['id']}#{time.time_ns()}"                                   # unique per attempt, so a re-take never overwrites an earlier charge
        led.reserve(jid, j["credits"])
        try:
            data, hdr = post("POST", f"/v1/text-to-speech/{j['voice_id']}?output_format=mp3_44100_128", key, {"text": j["text"], "model_id": j["model"], **({"voice_settings": j["settings"]} if j.get("settings") else {})})
            h = {k.lower(): v for k, v in hdr.items()}
            confirmed = "character-cost" in h
            used = int(h["character-cost"]) if confirmed else j["credits"]
            f.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
            f.write_bytes(data)
            secs = probe(f)                                                      # a 200 reply is not audio until it decodes
            if not 0.3 <= secs <= 90:
                raise RuntimeError(f"implausible duration {secs:.2f} s")
            led.settle(jid, used, confirmed)
            row.update(ok=True, file=str(f.relative_to(out)).replace("\\", "/"), mp3_sha256=sha256_file(f), seconds=round(secs, 3), credits_used=used, credits_confirmed=confirmed)
            rows[j["key"]] = row
            _save({"status": "DRAFT, NOT VALIDATED until the owner has listened", "lines": list(rows.values())}, mpath)      # checkpoint after every clip
        except RuntimeError as exc:                                          # the reservation stays open: the owner must look at the usage page
            row.update(ok=False, error=str(exc).replace(key, "[key]"))
            failed = row
            break
    man = {"status": "DRAFT, NOT VALIDATED until the owner has listened", "lines": list(rows.values()) + ([failed] if failed else []), "ok": len(rows), "reused": reused,
           "credits_committed": led.committed(), "credits_unconfirmed_clips": led.unconfirmed()}
    _save(man, mpath)
    return man


def measured(man: dict, plan: dict, script_sha256: str, model: str) -> dict:
    """The measured-durations file in the shape a1_audio.py expects, from the accepted clips of a run: every line of the plan needs a clip in both languages."""
    clips = {}
    for r in latest_ok(man):
        if True:
            clips[r["id"]] = {"lang": r["lang"], "voice": r["voice"], "speaker": r["voice_id"], "seconds": r["seconds"], "mp3_sha256": r["mp3_sha256"], "text": r["text"], "key": r["key"]}
    lines, problems = {}, []
    for l in plan["lines"]:
        for lang in LANGS:
            c = clips.get(f"{l['id']}.{lang}")
            if not c:
                problems.append(f"{l['id']}.{lang}: no accepted clip")
            elif c["voice"] != l["voice"]:                                   # a take in another voice never counts (owner 2026-11-01: speaker changes)
                problems.append(f"{l['id']}.{lang}: clip voice {c['voice']} but the plan says {l['voice']}")
            else:
                lines.setdefault(l["id"], {})[lang] = c["seconds"]
    return {"status": "MEASURED from ElevenLabs speech (DRAFT voices, NOT VALIDATED until the owner has listened)", "engine": "elevenlabs", "model": model, "script_sha256": script_sha256,
            "problems": problems, "clips": clips, "lines": lines}


def latest_ok(man: dict) -> list:
    """One accepted clip per line id: the NEWEST one (a re-generated line with new text or speed replaces the earlier clip in the mix; the earlier file stays on disk)."""
    d = {}
    for r in man["lines"]:
        if r.get("ok"):
            d[r["id"]] = r
    return list(d.values())


MAX_TEMPO = 1.15                                                                            # local speed-up limit (owner 2026-11-09: up to about 20 pct is acceptable; texts are sized for 1.08); the accepted mp3 is never modified
TRIM = "silenceremove=start_periods=1:start_threshold=-45dB,areverse,silenceremove=start_periods=1:start_threshold=-45dB,areverse"      # cuts only the silence at both ends of the wav copy


def load_slots(pack: Path, windows: Path | None = None) -> dict:
    """{line id: slot seconds} from the pack: the time window each line owns in its shot.
    windows = optional FINAL_TEXT_v2.json ({"<line>.<lang>": {"window_s": ..}}): the audio window (free time inside the shot) replaces the scripted speaking window."""
    out = {}
    for s in json.loads((pack / "shots.json").read_text(encoding="utf-8")):
        a = s["audio_and_dialogue_track"]
        if a["narration_by_lang"]["en"].get("text"):
            t = a["narration_by_lang"]["en"]["time_range"]
            out[s["id"] + "-N"] = t[1] - t[0]
        for k, d in enumerate(a["dialogue_by_lang"]["en"], 1):
            out[s["id"] + "-D" + str(k)] = d["time_range"][1] - d["time_range"][0]
    if windows and Path(windows).exists():
        for k, v in json.loads(Path(windows).read_text(encoding="utf-8")).items():
            out[k.rsplit(".", 1)[0]] = v["window_s"]
    return out


def fit_report(man: dict, slots: dict) -> list:
    """One row per accepted clip: measured seconds, slot, tempo needed (>1 = too long), verdict. A too-long clip is fitted locally up to MAX_TEMPO; beyond that it is reported, never regenerated."""
    rows = []
    for r in latest_ok(man):
        if True:
            slot = slots[r["line"]]
            tempo = max(1.0, r["seconds"] / slot)
            rows.append({"id": r["id"], "seconds": r["seconds"], "slot": round(slot, 2), "tempo": round(tempo, 3), "verdict": "fits" if tempo == 1.0 else ("fit by atempo" if tempo <= MAX_TEMPO else "TOO LONG: owner decision")})
    return rows


def export_wavs(man: dict, out: Path, wav_dir: Path, model: str, rate: int = 44100, slots: dict | None = None, report: list | None = None) -> int:
    """Decode every accepted clip to mono 16-bit wav named <line>.<lang>.wav (the layout a1_voice.py mix reads), edge silence cut (TRIM); with slots, a clip longer than its slot
    (measured on the trimmed wav) is sped up by at most MAX_TEMPO in the wav copy. report (a list) receives one row per clip: trimmed seconds, slot, tempo, verdict."""
    n = 0
    for r in latest_ok(man):
        dst = wav_dir / "wav" / r["lang"] / f"{r['id']}.wav"
        dst.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        subprocess.run(["ffmpeg", "-y", "-v", "error", "-i", str(out / r["file"]), "-ac", "1", "-ar", str(rate), "-sample_fmt", "s16", "-af", TRIM, str(dst)], check=True)
        if slots:
            secs, slot = probe_seconds(dst), slots[r["line"]]
            tempo = max(1.0, secs / slot)
            if 1.0 < tempo <= MAX_TEMPO:
                tmp = dst.with_name(dst.stem + ".fit.wav")
                subprocess.run(["ffmpeg", "-y", "-v", "error", "-i", str(dst), "-af", f"atempo={tempo:.4f}", str(tmp)], check=True)
"""Per-language editorial lengths (music session decisions, 2026-11-09): the file `<pack>/editorial_by_lang.json`.

ONE shared timeline: every language gets the same values (one video, 3 audio tracks, one score). A shot grows only by frames the clip
already has (spare tail; the last shot may only grow at its START); nothing is regenerated. Missing file = the v3 build, unchanged.

  {"fps": 24, "by_lang": {"en": {"SHOT-005": {"extend_frames": 12, "at": "end"}, ...}, "hi": {...same...}, "mr": {...same...}}}

Plan (writes the file): for each shot, the largest need of all languages = the length at which the voice plays at natural speed and ends
TAIL s before the cut; extra time rounded UP to whole beats for the shots given in --beats (BPM), not rounded for the others; capped by the
clip's spare frames; when rounding up does not fit, round DOWN and accept a voice speed-up of at most 1.03 (else reported).

  python editorial_by_lang.py --pack <pack> --story <h3_story.json> --raw <root with <lang>/<line>.<lang>.wav> --langs en,hi,mr
         --beats SHOT-003:128,SHOT-004:128,SHOT-006:176,SHOT-007:176,SHOT-008:176 [--write]
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import copy
import json
import math
import sys
from pathlib import Path

HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
sys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))
from build_vo_tracks import TAIL, pack_shot, scripted_lines, wav_seconds  # noqa: E402

FILE = "editorial_by_lang.json"
MAX_SPEEDUP = 1.03


def load(pack):
    """The shared per-shot extensions {shot: (frames, at)}, or {} when the file is missing. Languages must agree (one timeline)."""
    p = Path(pack) / FILE
    if not p.is_file():
        return {}
    doc = json.loads(p.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    langs = list(doc["by_lang"].values())
    if any(x != langs[0] for x in langs):
        raise ValueError(f"{p}: languages differ; only one shared timeline is supported")
    return {s: (int(v["extend_frames"]), v.get("at", "end")) for s, v in langs[0].items() if int(v["extend_frames"])}


def apply_rows(rows, ext, fps=24):
    out = copy.deepcopy(rows)
    for r in out:
        if r["id"] in ext:
            r["editorial_duration_sec"] = round(float(r["editorial_duration_sec"]) + ext[r["id"]][0] / fps, 4)
    return out


def apply_shots(h3_shots, ext):
    """New trim window, editorial length and master-reel windows of the H3 shots (copies)."""
    out, cum = copy.deepcopy(h3_shots), 0
    for s in out:
        t = s["timing_and_lattice"]
        n, at = ext.get(s["shot_id"], (0, "end"))
        fps = t["fps"]
        if at == "start":
            if n > t["trim_in_frame"]:
                raise ValueError(f"{s['shot_id']}: needs {n} head frames, clip has {t['trim_in_frame']}")
            t["trim_in_frame"] -= n
        else:
            if t["trim_out_frame"] + n > t["pixel_frames"]:
                raise ValueError(f"{s['shot_id']}: needs {n} tail frames, clip has {t['pixel_frames'] - t['trim_out_frame']}")
            t["trim_out_frame"] += n
        t["editorial_frames"] = t["trim_out_frame"] - t["trim_in_frame"]
        t["editorial_duration_sec"] = round(t["editorial_frames"] / fps, 4)
        t["trim_in_sec"], t["trim_out_sec"] = round(t["trim_in_frame"] / fps, 4), round(t["trim_out_frame"] / fps, 4)
        t["master_reel_frame_window"] = [cum, cum + t["editorial_frames"]]
        t["master_reel_window_sec"] = [round(cum / fps, 4), round((cum + t["editorial_frames"]) / fps, 4)]
        cum += t["editorial_frames"]
    return out


def needed_sec(lines, tempo):
    """Shot length at which these lines, packed at exactly `tempo`, end TAIL s before the cut."""
    sped = [dict(x, natural=x["natural"] / tempo) for x in lines]
    _, placed = pack_shot(sped, 1e9, max_tempo=1.0)
    return max(p["end"] for p in placed) + TAIL


def plan_shot(need1, need_max, editorial, spare, fps, beat=None):
    """Frames to add. need1 = length for natural speed, need_max = length at MAX_SPEEDUP. Returns (frames, note)."""
    raw = need1 - editorial
    if raw <= 1e-9:
        return 0, "fits at natural speed"
    if beat:
        frames = round(math.ceil(raw / beat - 1e-9) * beat * fps)
        if frames <= spare:
            return frames, f"rounded up to {round(frames / fps / beat)} beat(s)"
        frames = int(math.floor(spare / fps / beat) * beat * fps)
        note = f"rounded down to {round(frames / fps / beat)} beat(s) (spare {spare} fr)"
    else:
        frames = math.ceil(raw * fps - 1e-9)
        if frames <= spare:
            return frames, "natural speed, not rounded"
        frames, note = spare, f"all spare frames ({spare})"
    if editorial + frames / fps + 1e-9 < need_max:
        note += f"; VOICE STILL ABOVE {MAX_SPEEDUP}x"
    return frames, note


def plan(rows, h3_shots, raw_root, langs, beats_bpm):
    shots = {s["shot_id"]: s["timing_and_lattice"] for s in h3_shots}
    out, report = {}, []
    for i, r in enumerate(rows):
        sid, t = r["id"], shots[r["id"]]
        fps, ed = t["fps"], float(r["editorial_duration_sec"])
        last = i == len(rows) - 1
        need1 = need_max = 0.0
        for lg in langs:
            sl = scripted_lines(r, lg)
            if sl:
                lines = [{"id": k, "start": s, "natural": wav_seconds(Path(raw_root) / lg / f"{k}.{lg}.wav")} for k, s in sl]
